      "id": "plans_2026_06_09_google_login_plan",
      "label": "Sign in with Google Plan (Model A)",
      "file_type": "concept",
      "source_file": "plans/2026-06-09-google-login.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Auth.js v5 with the Google provider, JWT sessions (stateless, keeps proxy.ts simple, no DB writes per request), no DB migration (users not persisted until Model B), and an allow-list signIn callback as the security crux since Google sign-in is otherwise open to any Google account."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_09_google_login_model_a",
      "label": "Model A Identity Layer",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "plans/2026-06-09-google-login.md",
      "source_location": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Passcode + Google coexistence is safe only because Model A applies no per-user access scoping \u2014 a passcode user and a Google user get the same access to the shared households. The 'passcode + Google = foot-gun' warning only applies once households become per-user (Model B), at which point the plan said the passcode must be removed (it was later repurposed as an explicit superadmin instead)."
    },
